// ===========================================================================
// Syncthing ignore patterns for the shared drive.
//
// Install as `.stignore` in the ROOT of the synced folder — on the VPS that is
// ${WEBDAV_DATA_DIR}/.stignore (i.e. /opt/jvb/webdav-plain/.stignore).
//
// Syncthing syncs .stignore between devices only if you ask it to; simplest is
// to place the same file on the server and on each Mac. See infra/README.md §6f.
// ===========================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Cryptomator vaults — never synced.
//
// A vault is a directory of ciphertext. Syncing it is technically possible, but
// a vault that is unlocked on two machines at once can be corrupted: both sides
// write to the same internal files with no coordination, and Cryptomator has no
// multi-writer locking. Recovering from that means the passphrase no longer
// opens the vault, which is exactly the material you can least afford to lose.
//
// So: keep every vault under a single top-level Vaults/ directory, which lives
// on the server and is reached over the WebDAV mount only — one machine at a
// time, deliberately.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Vaults

// Belt and braces: catch a vault created outside Vaults/ by mistake. These are
// the two files at a vault's root, so ignoring them stops the vault being
// reassembled elsewhere even if the rest of its ciphertext were to sync.
vault.cryptomator
masterkey.cryptomator
masterkey.cryptomator.bkup

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// macOS metadata. Finder writes these constantly; without this they churn in
// both directions forever. (?d) lets Syncthing delete them when it would
// otherwise be blocked from removing an empty directory.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)._*
(?d).Spotlight-V100
(?d).Trashes
(?d).fseventsd
(?d).TemporaryItems
(?d).apdisk

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Office lock and scratch files — transient, and syncing them causes conflicts
// when two people have the same workbook open.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*
.~lock.*#
*.tmp
*.crdownload
*.part

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Syncthing's own version history (server side). Never send it to clients — it
// is the recovery copy, and replicating it would multiply the drive's size.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.stversions
